# gitleaks fingerprints to suppress, one per line.
#
# Keep this list short and each entry justified. A fingerprint is
# `<commit>:<file>:<rule>:<line>`, so it suppresses one finding in one commit
# and nothing else. Prefer this over widening .gitleaks.toml's regexes, which
# would blind the scan to a whole class of string everywhere.
#
# 6d09df0 — the regression guard in src/test/build-config.test.ts first named the
# old Supabase publishable key as a single literal. That key is public by design
# (row-level security protects the data, not the key) and .gitleaks.toml already
# allowlists the full `sb_publishable_...` form; it was flagged only because the
# literal was a 15-character truncated prefix, below that pattern's {20,} bound.
# The file no longer holds any key literal at all — it now matches the key's
# shape instead — so nothing current is being hidden. The commit is already
# pushed, and rewriting published history is not permitted, so the one historical
# finding is recorded here.
